---
import PageLayout from '@layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '2026-11-27';
const lastUpdatedLabel = '27 November 2026';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What openfinance-os.org collects when you visit, where it goes, and how to opt out."
>
  <div class="privacy-page">
    <article class="privacy-container">
      <header class="page-intro privacy-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
        <h1>What this site collects</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Open Finance OS is a community site. We count visits to learn which pages help people, and
          we hold your email address only if you subscribe to the newsletter. We do not sell data,
          run advertising or build profiles of individual visitors.
        </p>
        <p class="updated">
          Last updated <time datetime={lastUpdated}>{lastUpdatedLabel}</time>
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="analytics-title">
        <h2 id="analytics-title">Usage analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We use{' '}
          <a href="https://posthog.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            PostHog
          </a>
          , hosted in the United States, to measure how the site is used. While you browse, it
          records:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>the pages you view and when you leave them</li>
          <li>clicks on links and buttons, how far you scroll and how long a page stays open</li>
          <li>the words you type into site search, once you have typed three characters</li>
          <li>the site or campaign link that brought you here</li>
          <li>page loading times, and script errors that help us find broken pages</li>
          <li>
            your browser, device type and approximate location, which PostHog derives from your IP
            address
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          PostHog keeps a random identifier in your browser's session storage so that the pages of
          one visit can be counted together. It is deleted when you close the tab. The site sets no
          analytics cookies, does not record your session on screen, and shows no surveys. Apart
          from search, text you type into forms is not recorded.
        </p>
        <p>
          The <a href="/learn/readiness">readiness worksheet</a> loads no analytics at all. The
          <a href="/observatory/watch">Watch</a> page records only page views and which section or
          source you open.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="opt-out-title">
        <h2 id="opt-out-title">How to opt out</h2>
        <p>
          Turn on Do Not Track in your browser and the site stops sending analytics. Content
          blockers that block PostHog work too. The site works the same either way.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="newsletter-title">
        <h2 id="newsletter-title">Newsletter</h2>
        <p>
          When you subscribe, your email address goes to
          <a href="https://buttondown.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Buttondown
          </a>
          , which sends the weekly briefing for us. We use it only for that briefing. Every email
          has an unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing removes you from the list. Our analytics
          records that a signup form was submitted, never the address.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="browser-title">
        <h2 id="browser-title">What stays in your browser</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Your light or dark theme choice, kept in local storage until you clear it.</li>
          <li>
            The campaign link and referring site for the current visit, kept in session storage and
            deleted when you close the tab.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Earlier versions of the site kept a visitor ID and visit count in local storage, and
          PostHog kept its identifier in a cookie. The site now deletes both when you next visit.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="providers-title">
        <h2 id="providers-title">Other services that see your request</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Cloudflare hosts the site and processes each request, including your IP address, to
            deliver pages.
          </li>
          <li>Google Fonts serves the monospace font, so Google receives your IP address.</li>
          <li>
            Links to GitHub, Slack and official sources take you to sites with their own privacy
            terms.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
        <h2 id="contact-title">Questions</h2>
        <p>
          Ask in
          <a
            href="https://github.com/openfinance-os/community-website/discussions"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            GitHub Discussions
          </a>
          . The code that does all of this is public in the
          <a href="https://github.com/openfinance-os/community-website" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            site's repository
          </a>
          , so you can check this notice against it.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-5) var(--space-16);
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }
  .privacy-container {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .privacy-intro {
    padding: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .privacy-intro h1 {
    color: var(--color-brand-ink);
    font-size: clamp(2.15rem, 4.4vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .updated {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }
  .privacy-section {
    padding: var(--space-8) 0 0;
  }
  .privacy-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    color: var(--color-brand-ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .privacy-section p,
  .privacy-section li {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .privacy-section p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .privacy-section ul {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
  }
  .privacy-section a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
  }
</style>
